<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bir el Qutt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th–6th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bir el Qutt is the site of a Georgian monastery of the fifth and sixth centuries near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bethlehem">Bethlehem</a>, excavated in the 1950s. Its mosaic floors carry some of the earliest dated inscriptions in the Georgian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asomtavruli">Asomtavruli</a> script and show the early presence of Georgian monks in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-land">Holy Land</a>.</p></div>
